{"parentUuid":"6bf3c73d-3673-4caa-a033-eaf87c174a36","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGGmHzq1yWTYRwQumsYL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added one commit to `hedgerow-grass`, not pushed: fb292a6c, bullets crack the glass of the lit windows. Shaders compile on all three presets, node checks pass, and the merge with `hedgerow-poc` is still clean.\n\n- **The problem:** a shot into a lit window left a stone chip floating in front of it, as if the glass were wall.\n- **The fix:**\n  - The game now knows where every lit pane is in the world: 42 in the village.\n  - A hit within a pane's outline and up to 60 cm in front of it puts the mark on the glass itself.\n  - The new mark is a small dark hole in crushed white glass, with a star of cracks running out and shorter ring cracks between them. The cracks glow faintly with the warm room light behind, so they read against the bright window.\n- **Verified:** three shots into a ground-floor pane gave three cracks on the glass. A shot 1.6 m to the side stayed a stone hole.\n- **Limit:** only the lit windows know their glass. Dark windows are painted into the wall texture, so hits there still chip it as stone.\n\nAll test servers are stopped, no browser tabs are open, and my `launch.json` entry is removed. Notes are in the shared notes file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":230,"cache_read_input_tokens":743870,"output_tokens":407,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":230,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":407,"cache_read_input_tokens":743870,"cache_creation_input_tokens":230,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,