{"parentUuid":"18513928-2638-4154-8c4b-f21703162526","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGHLxs5v63e8A3a5VWV7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added one commit to `hedgerow-grass`, not pushed: 81e11279, muzzle flashes and grenade blasts that cast shadows, like modern Call of Duty's flash lights. Shaders compile on all three presets, node checks pass, and the merge with `hedgerow-poc` is still clean.\n\n- **The problem:** gun and grenade flashes lit the scene without shadows, so their light went straight through soldiers, sandbags and walls. A grenade behind a sandbag wall lit a glossy streak of cobbles on your side of it, and a man firing past another cast no shadow of him.\n- **The fix:** on high quality, the brightest flash near you briefly takes over the second shadow light for its few frames, and the street lamp it displaces lights without a shadow until it ends. Medium and low are unchanged.\n- **Verified by A/B against the committed lighting:**\n  - A flash behind a soldier now throws his long shadow across the wet cobbles toward you.\n  - Sandbags now shade the street in front of them from a blast behind.\n  - Your own shot looks the same apart from a faint shadow of the gun across the hand.\n- **Cost:** none measurable (21.85 vs 21.90 ms with a blast holding the light), because that shadow map was already redrawn every frame.\n\nAll test servers are stopped, no browser tabs are open, and my `launch.json` entry is removed. Notes are in the shared notes file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":248,"cache_read_input_tokens":793219,"output_tokens":473,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":248,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"infere