{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"19fa24d39dca1bbd9e2ca6bf09f20324d02d15903d9328709b755d0750295e56","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now the placement in damage.js: collect every exposed house side with a big enough open stretch of plaster 2.4–4.8 m up, then put signs on the most exposed few, spread out."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UvR3rbHdvZS5TmVRtK1uRG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='js/damage.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"  const sides = new Map(), colours = new Map(), tmp = {};\n  let breaks = 0, holes = 0;\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"  const sides = new Map(), colours = new Map(), tmp = {};\n  let breaks = 0, holes = 0;\n  const signs = [];\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"\"\"      // plaster blown off, bigger nearer the ground (the break fills an ellipse 0.94 by 0.62 of its\n      // decal; a smaller one where a big one will not fit)\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"      // where an old painted advertisement could be: high on a house's open plaster (the sign fills\n      // 0.94 by 0.42 of its decal)\n      if (PLASTERED.test(name) && exposed > 0.3) {\n        const hw = Math.ceil(SIGN * 0.47 / STEP), hh = Math.ceil(SIGN * 0.21 / STEP);\n        for (let t = 0; t < 60; t++) {\n          const cell = pick(2.4, 4.8);\n          if (cell < 0) break;\n          const i = cell % s.W, j = (cell / s.W) | 0;\n          if (!fits(s, i, j, hw, hh, true)) continue;\n          at(s, cell, tmp);\n          signs.push({ x: tmp.x, y: tmp.y, z: tmp.z, nx, nz, size: SIGN * k, exposed });\n          break;\n        }\n      }\n      // plaster blown off, bigger nearer the ground (the break fills an ellipse 0.94 by 0.62 of its\n      // decal; a smaller one where a big one will not fit)\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"\"\"  return { breaks, holes };\n}\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"  // the advertisements: on the most exposed of those walls, no two within 20 m, each a different\n  // trade as far as they go\n  signs.sort((a, b) => b.exposed - a.exposed);\n  const put = [];\n  for (const g of signs) {\n    if (put.length >= SIGNS) break;\n    if (put.some((o) => Math.hypot(o.x - g.x, o.z - g.z) < 20)) continue;\n    if (decals.pin('sign', g.x, g.y, g.z, g.nx, 0, g.nz, g.size, false, R, true, put.length)) put.push(g);\n  }\n  return { breaks, holes, signs: put.length };\n}\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"\"\"const SIDES = [[1, 0], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [0, -1]];\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"const SIDES = [[1, 0], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [0, -1]];\nconst SIGN = 3.7, SIGNS = 5;       // a painted advertisement's width (m), and how many\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"\"\"   How many marks a wall gets goes by how open the ground in front of it is\n   and how near that is to the lines the fighting follows.\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"   How many marks a wall gets goes by how open the ground in front of it is\n   and how near that is to the lines the fighting follows. High on the most\n   exposed houses' plaster, a few old painted advertisements, which the\n   breaks and the bursts go through.\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='js/main.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"  G.decals = createDecals({ shared, pinned: { stone: 480, wood: 80, spall: 64 } });\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"  G.decals = createDecals({ shared, pinned: { stone: 480, wood: 80, spall: 64, sign: 5 } });\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nfor f in damage main atmosphere; do cp js/$f.js $TMPDIR/chk_$f.mjs; node --check $TMPDIR/chk_$f.mjs && echo \"$f ok\"; rm -f $TMPDIR/chk_$f.mjs; done; grep -n \"exposed\\b\" js/damage.js | head -5","description":"Place the signs from damage.js and give them pinned room"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
