{"parentUuid":"e8b03d4a-24ae-488d-a395-dd20355c3b73","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGJ7TGMcMYgFMJCVVmC3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added one commit to `hedgerow-grass`, not pushed: c83f31ec, old painted advertisements on the village gables. Shaders compile on all three presets, node checks pass, and the merge with `hedgerow-poc` is still clean.\n\n**Measuring against AAA:** the stop hook keeps pointing out that nothing compares the game to Call of Duty or Medal of Honor, so I wrote a feature-by-feature gap list into the shared notes.\n- Hedgerow now has nearly every rendering system those games show: shadowed lights, screen-space reflections and ambient occlusion, light in the fog, rain systems, surface decals, particles, fire, water, and close-up material detail.\n- The gaps left:\n  - **Asset fidelity**, mainly the low-poly first-person hands and soldiers. They're assets and the rig, outside this branch's brief.\n  - **No bounce lighting** off walls.\n  - **Nothing destructible.**\n  - **No cloth**, such as flags, curtains or tarps.\n  - **Little environment storytelling.**\n  - **Two calls I left to you:** blood, and how hard enemies are to see at night.\n\n**This round's improvement** closes the storytelling gap a little.\n- **What you see:** the most exposed houses now carry faded painted advertisements high on their gables, as French village gables did: VINS FINS, QUINQUINA, CAFÉ · TABAC, ÉPICERIE. The trades are generic; no brand names.\n- **Look:** the paint is faded enough that the plaster's rain streaks show through, flaked at the edges, and washed thin in streaks. Old plaster breaks and bullet bursts go through it.\n- **Placement:** each sign goes only on open, even plaster 2.6–4.9 m up, found the same way as the battle damage. Four fit in the village.\n- **Cost:** about 70 ms at load, nothing per frame.\n- **Side effect:** placing the signs shifted the battle-damage layout. It's still the same every load.\n\nAll test servers are stopped, no browser tabs are open, and my `launch.json` entry is removed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_read_input_tokens":852068,"output_tokens":702,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":226,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":852068,"cache_creation_input_tokens":226,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":226},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"72f9a217-cdfc-44ce-b4b9-c816dea3f081","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGJ7SXiKCNz14Mp5ex3u","requestRef":"7695dfb0-3854-4c9b-8a9b-43df8f1bf050","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"0064d3c0-0d30-455b-a866-9cf63e69fee9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:03:19.183Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
