{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","hash":"491ec70de9227fef28e2cd9f5d7df59898171001376c118521d38d9d990e2363","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I found that the fireball always draws over the dirt column due to render order, but the dirt needs to appear in front for a dark geyser effect. I'll check how particles are lit, since dirt lit from the front by the blast light would glow orange instead of reading dark.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FWg3QAFTJaH277LLErcQZt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && sed -n \"$(grep -n 'const VERT = /\\* glsl \\*/' js/effects.js | cut -d: -f1),+75p\" js/effects.js","description":"Read the particle vertex shader lighting"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
