{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","id":"a0b290ef-4448-49cd-86b1-c96dd937c5fd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:10:15.681Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"aca1d33e67df77c08846866245a8b157faabfdb8617ed3a1eb9cac3e5556c296","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"max"}},"base":"cf65b78e-fe7f-4624-b0ae-eda77b08e141","keep":1812,"tail":["9b419bf12a2bd10a13264c318a167bfe8c39a60f088f0c68953eb12f1b4d6be3","7221ee39ca4fa6051ec92571f016fc3d8344eecdf620a5d25235d2fb33fd52e5","82e46e44f8e545d63fc602090ca7ac257125cd9517fe4171a117860c694483d5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1814,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"0c83747d452d81021e2e32791f84c8a1a0b5b3a75b1c5f89e004e1e301697c58"}
{"parentUuid":"b6a913f8-071b-4625-ba98-a90df1de3412","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGJembHm7BcG1EYe65fu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017zm7oUNdTefaDby8RV2J2z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    cool; blasts throw up a\n    column of earth and roll dust along the ground; a shot or a step into\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    cool; a blast flashes for a frame or two and throws up a geyser of wet\n    mud in dark jets and a spray of it in streaks, drawn after its fireball\n    so the mud covers the fire it flies through, and rolls low dark spray\n    and smoke along the ground (mud and dirt are lit on the side facing a\n    light, so they stand dark against the fireball); a shot or a step into\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"\"\"    blast's fireball: a billboard whose shader swells a ball of turbulent\n    flame in a tenth of a second, yellow at its heart and orange in its\n    folds, cooling from the outside in to a dull red glow inside a ball of\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    blast's fireball: a billboard whose shader swells a ball of turbulent\n    flame in a tenth of a second, white only at its heart for a frame or\n    two, yellow and orange in its folds, cooling from the outside in from\n    the start to a dull red glow inside a ball of\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/js/fireball.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: a blast throws up a geyser of wet mud\n\nA grenade read as a ball of light, then a pale beige dust ring. Its\nfirst 80 ms were a big round white-hot orb: the fireball's whole inside\nat its hottest, a 2.2-3.5 m flash sprite and bloom. The column of earth\nit threw up was small, lit orange by the blast, and drawn underneath the\nfireball, which is in the late pass. In Call of Duty a ground blast is\na sharp, brief flash with a dark dirt geyser thrown up through the fire.\nWet Normandy ground would throw mud and spray, not dust.\n\nNow:\n - The flash sprite is briefer (0.045 s) and smaller (1.5-2.6 m), and\n   the fireball cools from the start, so it is white only at its heart\n   for a frame or two and shows its orange folds sooner.\n - A third particle system in effects.js is drawn in the late pass after\n   the fireball (render order 6.5), so what a blast throws up covers the\n   fire it flies through. The mud geyser (30 dark jets in a fan, larger,\n   streaked along their flight) and a spray of fine mud in streaks go\n   there.\n - Particles get a 'dense' flag. Mud and dirt are lit only on the side\n   facing a light (down to 15% when the light is behind them), so they\n   stand dark against the fireball instead of glowing orange with it.\n   Smoke stays lit from all round.\n - The dust rolling out along the ground is darker and lower: wet\n   spray and smoke.\nWater blasts are as before. Low quality, which has no late pass, draws\nthe same with the scene.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merge with hedgerow-poc: clean\"","description":"Commit the blast rework and check the merge"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1068,"cache_read_input_tokens":899739,"output_tokens":1327,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1068,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1327,"cache_read_input_tokens":899739,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1068},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017zm7oUNdTefaDby8RV2J2z":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    cool; blasts throw up a\n    column of earth and roll dust along the ground; a shot or a step into\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    cool; a blast flashes for a frame or two and throws up a geyser of wet\n    mud in dark jets and a spray of it in streaks, drawn after its fireball\n    so the mud covers the fire it flies through, and rolls low dark spray\n    and smoke along the ground (mud and dirt are lit on the side facing a\n    light, so they stand dark against the fireball); a shot or a step into\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nold=\"\"\"    blast's fireball: a billboard whose shader swells a ball of turbulent\n    flame in a tenth of a second, yellow at its heart and orange in its\n    folds, cooling from the outside in to a dull red glow inside a ball of\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    blast's fireball: a billboard whose shader swells a ball of turbulent\n    flame in a tenth of a second, white only at its heart for a frame or\n    two, yellow and orange in its folds, cooling from the outside in from\n    the start to a dull red glow inside a ball of\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git add fun/hedgerow/README.md fun/hedgerow/js/effects.js fun/hedgerow/js/fireball.js && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nHedgerow graphics: a blast throws up a geyser of wet mud\n\nA grenade read as a ball of light, then a pale beige dust ring. Its\nfirst 80 ms were a big round white-hot orb: the fireball's whole inside\nat its hottest, a 2.2-3.5 m flash sprite and bloom. The column of earth\nit threw up was small, lit orange by the blast, and drawn underneath the\nfireball, which is in the late pass. In Call of Duty a ground blast is\na sharp, brief flash with a dark dirt geyser thrown up through the fire.\nWet Normandy ground would throw mud and spray, not dust.\n\nNow:\n - The flash sprite is briefer (0.045 s) and smaller (1.5-2.6 m), and\n   the fireball cools from the start, so it is white only at its heart\n   for a frame or two and shows its orange folds sooner.\n - A third particle system in effects.js is drawn in the late pass after\n   the fireball (render order 6.5), so what a blast throws up covers the\n   fire it flies through. The mud geyser (30 dark jets in a fan, larger,\n   streaked along their flight) and a spray of fine mud in streaks go\n   there.\n - Particles get a 'dense' flag. Mud and dirt are lit only on the side\n   facing a light (down to 15% when the light is behind them), so they\n   stand dark against the fireball instead of glowing orange with it.\n   Smoke stays lit from all round.\n - The dust rolling out along the ground is darker and lower: wet\n   spray and smoke.\nWater blasts are as before. Low quality, which has no late pass, draws\nthe same with the scene.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && git merge-tree --write-tree hedgerow-poc hedgerow-grass >/dev/null && echo \"merge with hedgerow-poc: clean\"","description":"Commit the blast rework and check the merge"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_017zm7oUNdTefaDby8RV2J2z":{"cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1951e923-af8f-45bf-8f1b-d8cb8767ab26","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGJekxLt4f9JNj6WdTiH","requestRef":"a0b290ef-4448-49cd-86b1-c96dd937c5fd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant",