{"parentUuid":"b56a570f-13be-4390-88f1-e4ddf8b3029e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGJiYz7nZUbrtrpd8sAd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added one commit to `hedgerow-grass`, not pushed: ca04193d, grenades throw up a geyser of wet mud. Shaders compile on all three presets, node checks pass, and the merge with `hedgerow-poc` is still clean.\n\nI compared the burning truck and a grenade, frame by frame, with how Call of Duty draws a ground blast. The truck fire holds up. The grenade didn't:\n- For its first 80 ms it was a big round white ball.\n- Then it became pale beige dust.\n- The dirt it threw up was small, lit orange, and drawn underneath the fireball.\n\nNow:\n- **Flash:** briefer and smaller, and the fireball is white only at its heart for a frame or two, so it no longer reads as a light bulb.\n- **Mud geyser:** dark jets of wet mud, plus a spray of fine mud, are drawn after the fireball, so they cover the fire they fly through. By 0.6 s a dark column carries the red glow inside it.\n- **Dark against the fire:** mud and dirt are lit only on the side facing a light, so they stand dark against the fireball instead of glowing orange. Smoke is lit as before.\n- **Ground spray:** what rolls out along the ground is darker and lower, wet spray and smoke rather than dust.\n- Water blasts are unchanged, and low quality, which has no late pass, still draws all of it.\n\nAll test servers are stopped, no browser tabs are open, and my `launch.json` entry is removed. Notes are in the shared notes file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":241,"cache_read_input_tokens":904031,"output_tokens":506,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":241,"e