{"parentUuid":"c937e250-a174-462d-b6e7-c0b165b3aefd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGKEQdvDShL2jaSGajLa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This round added one commit to `hedgerow-grass`, not pushed: 2a45e2e9, glass breaking out of a shot window. Shaders compile on all three presets, node checks pass, and the merge with `hedgerow-poc` is still clean.\n\n**Reference check:** the hook asks for a real comparison with Call of Duty or Medal of Honor, so I tried to pull actual frames from Call of Duty: Vanguard's \"Operation Tonga\", the closest match to this mission.\n- The wiki blocks opening its images directly, and its full-size viewer sits behind a cookie-consent wall.\n- Store pages with screenshots put M-rated games behind an age gate that asks for a birth date.\n- I didn't accept the consent or enter personal details, so the comparisons stay from what I know of those games. If you can drop a few reference screenshots into the scratch folder, I can compare frame by frame.\n\n**This round's improvement:**\n- **The problem:** a shot into a lit window cracked the glass (fb292a6c) but threw a beige puff of stone dust in front of the window, and nothing broke.\n- **The fix:** the impact effects now share the decals' knowledge of where the window panes are. A hit on a pane gives glass instead of stone: shards break out, lit by the room's light, a burst of bright flecks marks the hole, and glinting flecks fall with the shards.\n- **Verified:** the window stays clear of dust, and the shards land on the flower box below. The crack mark is unchanged.\n- **Still missing:** the sound is still the stone impact, since the game has no glass-breaking sound yet.\n\nAll test servers are stopped, no browser tabs are open, and my `launch.json` entry is removed. Notes are in the shared notes file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_read_input_tokens":944547,"output_tokens":575,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":254,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":575,"cache_read_input_tokens":944547,"cache_creation_input_tokens":254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":254},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"813b4d6f-6cb6-4e45-ac89-12c57bc52e4c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGKEPq3sxigJVkJRF6VF","requestRef":"cf12652a-5fbf-49ca-8a7d-44cd0ca05a9a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"0010e23f-17c8-48df-8aac-5df570e3bd3d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:17:58.289Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
