{"parentUuid":"99067f26-9517-440e-89c2-3518ca4224c6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Monitor, Read, SendMessage, TaskStop, ToolSearch, Write, mcp__Claude_Browser__computer, mcp__Claude_Browser__find, mcp__Claude_Browser__javascript_tool, mcp__Claude_Browser__navigate, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_list, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_start, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_stop, mcp__Claude_Browser__read_console_messages, mcp__Claude_Browser__resize_window, mcp__Claude_Browser__tabs_close, mcp__Claude_Browser__tabs_context, mcp__ccd_session__hand_off_to_session, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - This is a side session started by `local_7d29cad9-bdd3-4987-9ed1-e8d4d12a5721`. It works on the Hedgerow game (`fun/hedgerow`, three.js r185, no build step) in the worktree `/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass`, branch `hedgerow-grass`.\n   - Standing goal, enforced by a Stop hook that re-prompts after every turn: \"constantly and iteratively improve the game graphics towards aaa game (call of duty, medal of honor). commit each improvement.\"\n     - The hook keeps rejecting completion. It says the rounds are discrete, each ends in teardown, and nothing measures the game against Call of Duty or Medal of Honor.\n     - The working approach is verified rounds: each improvement is committed, then teardown and wrap_up, then the next round on re-prompt.\n   - Hard constraints from the hand-off, kept verbatim:\n     - \"commit only, never push\"\n     - \"Don't touch camera.js, player.js, hud.js or character.js. The original session is converting the game to first person in them, on branch hedgerow-poc.\"\n     - \"Never commit Blender preview renders.\"\n     - \"Add your own entry to /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/launch.json, and don't touch the main checkout's files otherwise.\"\n     - When done: stop the server, close the browser tab, remove the launch.json entry (rm needs dangerouslyDisableSandbox).\n   - Side-session rules:\n     - Commit only the files I changed.\n     - Never stash, reset or switch branches.\n     - Put what I did first in reports.\n     - Leave notes in the shared notes file: `/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md`.\n   - Memory rule: \"end every browser session and local server used for testing once done\".\n   - Commit messages: \"Hedgerow graphics: …\", ending with \"Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\".\n   - Safety and privacy rules applied this window:\n     - Do not accept cookie or consent banners; decline non-essential or leave them alone.\n     - Do not enter personal data such as a birth date for age gates.\n     - Reference images from external sites are viewed for analysis only, never reproduced.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Effects chain** via `renderer.setEffects`:\n     - Early `G.effects.pass`: particles drawn into the scene buffer with soft depth.\n     - Late pass `G.effects.late.scene`: after TAA, holding the additive particles, fireballs, rain, flames, drips and the new `thrown` system.\n     - Render orders: fireball 6, `thrown` 6.5, additive 7.\n   - **Lights** (lights.js):\n     - A pool of 8 point lights plus `shadowLight`, and `shadowLight2` on high quality (shadows >= 512).\n     - Statics are scored by intensity × range / (1 + d²).\n     - Flashes can now take `shadowLight2`.\n     - The light-loop culling patch (lightloop.js) is from before this window.\n   - **Decals** (atmosphere.js):\n     - Instanced quads, 2×2 variant atlases, PULL toward the eye.\n     - Pinned decals reserve fixed room per kind, so gameplay hits never recycle them.\n     - Kinds: stone, wood, metal, splat, scorch, glass, spall, sign.\n   - **damage.js** software raster of model sides: a 5 cm grid of depth, facing, lum and sat. `fits()` checks flatness (step test), darkness and plaster. Exposure comes from raycasts plus distance to the route lines.\n   - **Particle system** (effects.js):\n     - Arrays on the CPU and instanced attributes: aPos, aColor, aMisc (size, rot, cell, dense), aStretch.\n     - Lit by up to 8 lights at the sprite corners.\n     - New `dense` flag: mud and dirt are lit on the side facing a light.\n   - **GLSL helpers** (terrain.js `GLSL_HELPERS`):\n     - `rainRipples(p, t, fade)` has a new third argument.\n     - `rippleFade(dist)`, `cotangentFrame`, `hash12`.\n     - `GUST_GLSL` (weather.js): `gust(xz, time, wind)` returns 0.55–1.6.\n   - **Material patching** via `onBeforeCompile` in materials.js `addWeather` options: foliage, cover, bark, streaks, rooms, smoulder, skin, glints, grain, gun. Each option adds a letter to the cache key.\n   - **Interior-mapped lit windows** (rooms.js): panes are found in the emissive atlas, and their frames are now kept in `geometry.userData.panes`.\n   - **Headless testing**:\n     - Chrome headless shell over CDP via `scratchpad/hl.mjs`.\n     - Captures go through the `snap` and `snapCrop` POST endpoint into `scratchpad/snaps`.\n     - GPU timing uses `gpuMs` and `ab` from perf0.js.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all under `fun/hedgerow/js` unless noted):\n   - **lights.js (8dcfc434, 81e11279):** `createLighting(scene, { pool, shadows, shadowSize, second })`, a `shadowCaster()` factory, and `shadowLight2` when `shadows && second`. Flash shadows:\n     ```js\n     flashes.push({ x, y, z, color: new THREE.Color(color), intensity, range, life, age: 0, fog, flash: true, now: intensity, fogNow: fog });\n     // in update(), after static shadow selection:\n     for (let i = flashes.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) { const f = flashes[i]; f.age += dt; if (f.age >= f.life) { flashes.splice(i, 1); continue; }\n       f.now = f.intensity * (1 - f.age / f.life) ** 2;\n       const dc = Math.hypot(f.x - cam.x, f.y - cam.y, f.z - cam.z); const near = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (dc - 1.5) / 2.5));\n       f.fogNow = f.fog * (0.15 + 0.85 * near * near * (3 - 2 * near)); }\n     if (shadowLight2) { let fl = null, bf = 0;\n       for (const f of flashes) { const d2 = ...; if (d2 > 40 * 40) continue; const sc = f.now * f.range / (1 + d2); if (sc > bf) { bf = sc; fl = f; } }\n       if (fl && (!shadowOf2 || bf > best2 * 0.5)) { shadowOf2 = fl; best2 = bf; } }\n     // place(): if (s.flash) { l.position.set(s.x, s.y, s.z); l.intensity = s.now; } else {...wander/flick}\n     // cand: for (const f of flashes) { if (f === shadowOf2) continue; cand.push({..., intensity: f.now, score: 1e9, fog: f.fogNow }); }\n     // active entry for shadowOf2 includes fog: shadowOf2.flash ? shadowOf2.fogNow : undefined\n     ```\n   - **main.js (various):**\n     - Imports added for `dressWalls` (damage.js), `createSteam` (steam.js) and `paneRects` (rooms.js).\n     - The decals are created with pinned room:\n       ```js\n       G.decals = createDecals({ shared, pinned: { stone: 480, wood: 80, spall: 64, sign: 5 } });\n       ```\n     - Lights: `createLighting(..., second: (quality.shadows || 0) >= 512)`.\n     - Right after `buildLevel`:\n       ```js\n       dressWalls(G, built.props, LEVEL.lines);\n       G.decals.setPanes(paneRects(built.props));\n       G.effects.setPaneAt(G.decals.paneAt);\n       ```\n     - `G.steam = createSteam(G, shared.rain)`: updated after `G.chunks.update(dt)` and cleared on retry.\n     - `castShadows` handles `sl2`.\n   - **damage.js (new in 6bbd4fff, signs added in c83f31ec):**\n     - Constants: `STEP=0.05`, `TOP=5.5`, `BUILT=/^(house|barn|ruin|bunker)|^church$/`, `PLASTERED=/^house/`, `SIGN=[4.2,3.7,3.3]`, `SIGNS=5`.\n     - Functions: `texels`, `floats`, `rasterSide`, `fits(s,i,j,hw,hh,plaster)`, `sideOf`.\n     - `dressWalls(G, props, lines, {seed=1944})` returns `{breaks, holes, signs}`.\n     - Signs are collected per exposed house side (exposure > 0.3; `pick(2.6,4.9)`; plaster fit for the band 0.47×size by 0.21×size), sorted by exposure, kept 20 m apart, and pinned with:\n       ```js\n       decals.pin('sign', x, y, z, nx, 0, nz, size, false, R, true, put.length)\n       ```\n   - **atmosphere.js:**\n     - **Helpers:** `ragged(R,x,y,r,n,jag,sy=1)`; `decalSet(paint, seed, ground, relief, bare=false, cell=CELL)` calls `paint(p,R,cx,cy,S,i)`.\n     - **Painters:** stoneHole, woodHole, metalHole, mudSplat, glassCrack, wallAd (ADS: VINS FINS, QUINQUINA, CAFÉ · TABAC, ÉPICERIE), plasterBreak (rubble/bricks), scorchMark.\n     - **createDecals:**\n       - `createDecals({max=200, shared=null, pinned={}})`.\n       - Sets: stone, wood, metal, splat, scorch, glass; plus spall and sign when pinned.\n       - Capacity: scorch 24; spall and sign 0 + pinned; glass 60.\n       - Glass emissive `#ffcc94` ×0.9 via `emissiveMap = map`.\n       - Render order: sign 0.5, spall 1, others 2.\n     - **Placing:**\n       - `put(K,i,x,y,zz,nx,ny,nz,size,grain,R,upright=false,variant=-1)`.\n       - `pin(kind,...,size,grain=false,R=Math.random,upright=false,variant=-1)`.\n     - **Panes:** `paneAt(x,y,zz)` returns `{x,y,z,n}` within a pane rect and −0.1…0.6 m along n. `impact()` reroutes stone or wood hits to a `'glass'` decal.\n     - Returns `{ group, add, pin, impact, clear, setPanes, paneAt }`.\n   - **rooms.js (fb292a6c):**\n     - `pn.userData.panes = found.map(f => ({ c, n, T, B, hw, hh }))`.\n     - `export function paneRects(props)` transforms panes by `yaw` and `scale` into world positions. It returns 42 panes.\n   - **effects.js:**\n     - **Particle lighting and state:**\n       - The `dense` flag lives in aMisc.w; the VERT dims a light by `side` when that light is behind a dense particle.\n       - `P.dense` is set in `spawn` (`o.dense`), copied in `kill`, and written in `update`.\n     - **`thrown` system:**\n       ```js\n       const thrown = createSystem(600, atlas, false, fog, shared); thrown.mesh.renderOrder = 6.5;\n       ```\n       - It is added to `group`.\n       - `usePass` sets depthTest for alpha, add and thrown.\n       - `useLate` adds `add.mesh, thrown.mesh` to the late scene.\n       - It is updated each frame and included in `count`.\n     - **New emitters:**\n       - `leaves()` for foliage hits.\n       - `muzzle()` star plus flame tongues plus sparks.\n       - `glass(x,y,z,nx,nz)`: alpha shards plus 10 additive flecks.\n       - `steam(x,y,z,k)`.\n     - **impact():** routes water to splash, foliage to leaves, and stone or wood inside a pane (`paneAt`) to glass.\n     - **explosion():**\n       - Flash sprite: life 0.045, size 1.5→2.6.\n       - 30 dark mud jets in `thrown` (`#2c241b`, dense, streak 0.075).\n       - Dust ring `#433c33` a0.5.\n       - 34 mud spray streaks in `thrown`.\n     - Exports gained `steam`, `glass`, `setPaneAt(fn)`.\n   - **fireball.js (ca04193d):**\n     ```glsl\n     float cool = smoothstep(0.0, 0.55, t);\n     ```\n     It was `smoothstep(0.04, 0.7, t)`.\n   - **steam.js (new, 3a17285e):** `createSteam(G, rain)`.\n     - Heat rises by 0.12 per `'shot'` noise event, capped at 1.6, and decays by `exp(-dt/7)`.\n     - Emission rate is `dt*24*heat*rain`, along `muzzleWorld() - gunDir*t` for t in 0.03–0.43.\n     - Returns `{ update, clear }`.\n   - **weather.js (796b3fbe):**\n     - `SHEET_GLSL` holds `sheetStreak(...)` and `sheetLit(P)`; `SHEET_FRAG` uses it.\n     - New `SHELL_VERT`/`SHELL_FRAG` draw 4 cylinder meshes (64 segments, y −60..30).\n     - The shell is visible only when `!sheetsOn && n>0`; `uScreen` comes from `getDrawingBufferSize` in `onBeforeRender`.\n     - `GUST_GLSL` is exported (read this round for the cloth wind).\n   - **materials.js:**\n     - **Water material:** `vnoiseDW` swells; ripples faded with distance; rougher far off; scum line by distance to the edge.\n     - **Foliage:** `vFolTint`, `leafThin` ambient, `cover` option.\n     - **GUN:** regex plus `gun` option, wood grain and Parkerized steel with edge wear.\n     - **Skin variant:**\n       - Hand grime (`skNoise`, hand mask from the bind pose).\n       - Sleeve soak and mud.\n   - **terrain.js:** `rainRipples(p, t, fade)` with `p *= 2.4`, `phase t*1.3`, skipped when fade < 0.01; `rippleFade(dist) = 1 - smoothstep(8,16,dist)`; puddle ripples only where `tPuddle > 0.01`.\n   - **Other files:**\n     - **ssr.js:** passes `rippleFade(-P.z)`.\n     - **levelBuild.js:** crater squares added to the terrain's `fine` list.\n     - **groundmap.js:** pond keep is `smoothstep(0.03, 0.16, H - p.y)`.\n     - **ai.js:** `G.effects.impact(..., dir.x, dir.y, dir.z)`.\n   - **README.md:** updated for every commit.\n   - **Shared notes file:**\n     - Entries for each commit through 2a45e2e9.\n     - The AAA gap list, with gaps:\n       1. asset fidelity;\n       2. no bounce light;\n       3. nothing destructible;\n       4. no cloth;\n       5. storytelling;\n       6. blood (user call);\n       7. eye adaptation;\n       8. enemy readability (user call).\n     - The failed reference attempts.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Glass hit first spawned stone dust (the effects didn't know the panes) → added `effects.setPaneAt` and routing in `impact()`; the `onGlass` hook was removed.\n   - GLSL comment containing backticks inside a JS template → SyntaxError \"Unexpected identifier 'fade'\" and the game hung at boot → removed the backticks; diagnosed by importing modules in the page.\n   - damage.js fit test far too strict (2 cm flatness; plaster lum) → step test 1.2 cm per neighbour plus 5 cm overall; allow 8% off-plaster cells.\n   - Sign at 4.2 m fit only once → per-wall fallback sizes [4.2, 3.7, 3.3].\n   - Signs looked like enamel plaques, and a flake made \"BILLAPD\" → faded alpha, muted colours, flakes moved to edges and bottom.\n   - Wires: built.props has model objects while the level props have strings → used LEVEL.props; still invisible at honest thickness → dropped.\n   - The first steam puffs read as gun smoke → smaller streaked sprites.\n   - The hand grime debug view was masked by the existing skin debug overlays → use a negative `uSkinDebug` for the custom view.\n   - `hl.mjs stop` hit ENOTEMPTY removing hl-profile → wait for the process to exit, then `rm -rf hl-profile`.\n   - fs/hl captures: tag naming mismatches, file names like `sm2_2.jpg` vs `2.0` → adjusted the tilers.\n   - External references blocked: Fandom 403 hotlink blocking plus a consent wall (not accepted); Steam age gate (not entered).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Every improvement was verified with A/B captures and zoomed crops in headless Chrome, a per-preset compile check (q_chk2), the 9 node checks, and the merge-tree check against hedgerow-poc. All commits are clean merges.\n   - **Perf findings:**\n     - The second shadow light costs ~1–2.5 ms.\n     - Flash shadows cost nothing.\n     - Wall damage costs ~130 ms at load, signs +70 ms, low-quality rain shells within noise.\n   - **Dropped:** telegraph wires, smouldering craters, a soft-glow muzzle layer.\n   - **Left as user calls:** blood decals; enemy readability at night.\n   - **Reference comparison:** Medal of Honor: Airborne's Wikipedia frame (365×273, Italian dusk street) shows a large white hanging cloth. That is the basis for the current round, cloth (gap 4).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Only Stop hook feedback messages, repeating \"[constantly and iteratively improve the game graphics towards aaa game (call of duty, medal of honor). commit each improvement.]\".\n     - Each says the commit clause is met but the open-ended loop isn't sustained (rounds end in teardown).\n     - Each says no comparison against a Call of Duty or Medal of Honor standard is shown.\n     - The latest adds that the reference check failed, with no CoD/MoH frames viewed and comparisons resting on memory and self-written checklists.\n   - System reminders: \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\"\n   - One instruction: \"Your response above was cut off mid-stream. Resume directly from where it stops — no apology, no recap.\"\n   - The current summary request.\n   - The hand-off constraints quoted verbatim in section 1 remain in force.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Current round: implement wet white sheets hanging from lit upper-floor windows, moving in the wind (cloth, gap 4), then verify, check, document, take notes, commit and tear down.\n   - Continue further rounds on Stop hook re-prompts; commit each improvement; never push.\n   - Teardown each round:\n     - `node $S/hl.mjs stop` (dangerouslyDisableSandbox), then `rm -rf hl-profile`.\n     - `preview_stop` for the server.\n     - Close browser tabs.\n     - `rm /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/launch.json` (dangerouslyDisableSandbox).\n     - Confirm no headless processes, port 8766 free, and a clean git tree.\n   - Then call wrap_up, with what was done first.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - Round 17, toward the AAA reference.\n   - **Reference:** on Wikipedia, the CoD WWII image was only the daytime \"Headquarters\" hub, and the CoD Vanguard article has none. The Medal of Honor: Airborne frame `https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3b/MOHA_street.png` (365×273) shows:\n     - a dusk stone street with cobbles;\n     - sandbags and an MG position;\n     - a running enemy;\n     - a big white cloth hanging from an arch;\n     - a first-person Thompson.\n     - I closed the tab.\n   - **Decision:** add hanging wet white sheets from lit upper windows. During the fighting in Normandy, civilians hung white sheets from their windows.\n   - The plan was updated (the \"Hang wet white sheets from upper windows\" step is in progress), and I read `GUST_GLSL` (weather.js) and `dimFillSpecular(shader)` (fill.js).\n   - No cloth code is written yet. No rig is running: the launch.json entry was removed and the browser is closed.\n   - **Planned design** for a new `cloth.js`, `createSheets(panes, world, terrain, shared, { seed, count = 4 })`:\n     - **Pane choice:** pick panes from `paneRects(built.props)` (or `G.decals` panes) that are:\n       - upper floor (pane centre > ~4.5 m above `terrain.height`);\n       - in the street area (z 90–240, |x| < 15);\n       - facing the street (`n.x * (0 - c.x) > 0`);\n       - at most 4, more than 15 m apart, seeded.\n     - **Hanging line:** the top edge sits just below the sill (`c - B*hh`). It is pushed out to the wall face, found by a `G.world.raycast` toward −n, plus n×0.04.\n     - **Geometry:** one merged grid (~6×10 segments per sheet), width ≤ min(pane width×0.9, 1.2 m), height 1.3–1.7 m. It carries `uv` plus a per-vertex `aSheet` (n.x, n.z, phase, length).\n     - **Material:** `MeshStandardMaterial` with a canvas atlas (2×2 variants):\n       - off-white linen with water stains, a wet darker bottom and a frayed or torn alpha bottom edge;\n       - one variant with faint ticking stripes.\n       - `alphaTest 0.5`, `side: DoubleSide`, `flatShading: true`, roughness ~0.85 (wet ~0.7).\n     - **onBeforeCompile:**\n       - Vertex displacement uses `GUST_GLSL` and `shared.time`.\n       - `amp = v*v*(0.04 + 0.12*g)`.\n       - Displacement along n is outward only (≥ 0), with a sideways sway along T and small ripples.\n       - Also apply `dimFillSpecular(shader)`.\n     - **Shadows:** `castShadow` possibly false at first to avoid shadow-map mismatch; `receiveShadow` true.\n     - **Wiring:** in main.js after `G.decals.setPanes(...)`, and add the mesh to the scene.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - Continue the current round as stated just before this summary: \"So this round: wet white sheets hanging from a few lit upper-floor windows, moving with the wind's gusts.\"\n   - Then:\n     1. Write `js/cloth.js` and wire it in main.js.\n     2. Re-add my launch.json entry, start the preview server and the headless browser.\n     3. Capture street views of the sheets and iterate the look.\n     4. Run q_chk2 on low, medium and high, plus the 9 node checks.\n     5. Update the README and shared notes.\n     6. Commit as \"Hedgerow graphics: …\" with the Co-Authored-By line, and run the merge-tree check against hedgerow-poc.\n     7. Tear down: stop the headless browser, preview_stop, close tabs, remove the launch.json entry.\n     8. Call wrap_up, then the closing message with what was done first.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/vojta/.REDACTED.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"8f97cd88-a2b8-444c-85e1-ad0b89ae1c7e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:23:15.571Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":12,"turnIndex":45},"turnOrigin":"sdk","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["3d278cde-a1cb-4685-9ec4-6c132ee96e54"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"8f97cd88-a2b8-444c-85e1-ad0b89ae1c7e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/cloth.js","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow/js/cloth.js","content":"/* Hedgerow — white sheets hung from the windows.\n\n   While the fighting passed through their villages, Normandy's people hung\n   white sheets from their windows: there are people in here, not soldiers.\n   From a few of the lit upper-floor windows that look onto the street, a\n   sheet hangs over the sill and down the wall below it: old linen, stained,\n   its edge frayed or torn, soaked through by the rain, swinging and rippling\n   as the gusts that bend the trees go by (weather.js gust()), most at its\n   hem, and throwing its shadow on the wall from the lamps. One mesh, the\n   motion worked out in its vertex shader (and in its shadow's, so the two\n   stay together). */\n\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\nimport { GUST_GLSL } from './weather.js';\nimport { rng } from './util.js';\nimport { dimFillSpecular } from './fill.js';\n\nconst SX = 6, SY = 12;            // a sheet's quads across and down\n\n/* the linen, four ways (the quarters of the texture): plain, edged with ticking stripes, torn at a\n   corner, scalloped; stained, soiled along the hem, frayed. The canvas's rows run down the sheet */\nfunction linen() {\n  const S = 512, C = S / 2, R = rng(1944);\n  const c = document.createElement('canvas');\n  c.width = c.height = S;\n  const g = c.getContext('2d');\n  g.clearRect(0, 0, S, S);\n  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n    const x0 = (i % 2) * C, y0 = (i >> 1) * C;\n    g.save();\n    g.beginPath(); g.rect(x0, y0, C, C); g.clip();\n    // the cloth's outline: straight at the top (the hem over the sill), frayed or torn below\n    const path = new Path2D();\n    path.moveTo(x0, y0); path.lineTo(x0 + C, y0);\n    for (let k = 0; k <= 24; k++) {\n      const t = k / 24, x = x0 + C * (1 - t);\n      let y = y0 + C * (0.97 - 0.025 * R());\n      if (i === 3) y -= C * 0.03 * (0.5 + 0.5 * Math.cos(t * Math.PI * 12));     // scalloped\n      if (i === 2 && t < 0.35) y -= C * (0.35 - t) * 0.9 * (0.8 + 0.4 * R());     // torn away at a corner\n      path.lineTo(x, y);\n    }\n    path.closePath();\n    g.fillStyle = 'rgb(222,216,202)';\n    g.fill(path);\n    g.save(); g.clip(path);\n    // the weave, faint\n    for (let k = 0; k < 90; k++) {\n      g.fillStyle = `rgba(${R() < 0.5 ? '255,255,250' : '120,110,96'},${(0.03 + R() * 0.05).toFixed(3)})`;\n      if (R() < 0.5) g.fillRect(x0, y0 + R() * C, C, 1 + R() * 2); else g.fillRect(x0 + R() * C, y0, 1 + R() * 2, C);\n    }\n    // ticking stripes along its edges\n    if (i === 1) for (const xs of [0.08, 0.13, 0.87, 0.92]) { g.fillStyle = 'rgba(70,86,120,0.55)'; g.fillRect(x0 + C * xs, y0, C * 0.025, C); }\n    // stains: water marks with darker rims, and grime\n    for (let k = 0; k < 7; k++) {\n      const x = x0 + R() * C, y = y0 + C * (0.2 + R() * 0.75), r = C * (0.05 + R() * 0.14);\n      const gr = g.createRadialGradient(x, y, r * 0.5, x, y, r);\n      gr.addColorStop(0, 'rgba(180,160,120,0.10)'); gr.addColorStop(0.85, 'rgba(150,125,85,0.22)'); gr.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(150,125,85,0)');\n      g.fillStyle = gr; g.fillRect(x - r, y - r, 2 * r, 2 * r);\n    }\n    // soiled along the hem (the rain splashes it, the wall's grime runs into it), and the fold over the sill\n    const dirt = g.createLinearGradient(0, y0 + C * 0.65, 0, y0 + C);\n    dirt.addColorStop(0, 'rgba(90,72,50,0)'); dirt.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(90,72,50,0.45)');\n    g.fillStyle = dirt; g.fillRect(x0, y0, C, C);\n    g.fillStyle = 'rgba(80,70,58,0.25)'; g.fillRect(x0, y0 + C * 0.06, C, C * 0.012);\n    g.restore();\n    // frayed threads along the bottom\n    g.strokeStyle = 'rgba(222,216,202,0.9)'; g.lineWidth = 1;\n    for (let k = 0; k < 40; k++) {\n      const x = x0 + R() * C, y = y0 + C * 0.93;\n      g.beginPath(); g.moveTo(x, y); g.lineTo(x + (R() - 0.5) * 4, y + C * (0.01 + R() * 0.04)); g.stroke();\n    }\n    g.restore();\n  }\n  const t = new THREE.CanvasTexture(c);\n  t.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;\n  t.flipY = false;\n  t.anisotropy = 4;\n  return t;\n}\n\n/* the sheet's motion: hanging from its top edge, swinging out from the wall and along it as the gusts\n   go by, rippling across, most at its hem; never back into the wall. In the geometry's own space,\n   which is the world's */\nconst MOTION = /* glsl */ `\n  {\n    float hv = aSheet.y, hu = aSheet.x, ph = aFold.z;\n    vec3 n = vec3(aFold.x, 0.0, aFold.y), tw = vec3(aFold.y, 0.0, -aFold.x);\n    float g = gust(transformed.xz, uTime, uWind);\n    // a wet sheet is heavy: it swings less and clings\n    float a = hv * hv * (0.04 + 0.11 * g) * mix(1.0, 0.65, uWet);\n    float out = a * (0.55 + 0.45 * sin(uTime * 1.7 + ph + hv * 2.0)) + 0.02 * hv * g * (0.5 + 0.5 * sin(hu * 9.0 - uTime * 5.0 + ph));\n    float along = a * 0.6 * sin(uTime * 1.1 + ph * 1.7 + hv * 1.5);\n    transformed += n * out + tw * along;\n  }`;\n\nfunction addMotion(mat, uniforms) {\n  mat.onBeforeCompile = (shader) => {\n    Object.assign(shader.uniforms, uniforms);\n    shader.vertexShader = shader.vertexShader\n      .replace('#include <common>', `#include <common>\n        attribute vec4 aFold;\n        attribute vec2 aSheet;\n        uniform float uTime, uWet;\n        uniform vec2 uWind;\n        ${GUST_GLSL}`)\n      .replace('#include <begin_vertex>', '#include <begin_vertex>\\n' + MOTION);\n    if (mat.isMeshStandardMaterial) {\n      shader.fragmentShader = shader.fragmentShader\n        .replace('#include <common>', '#include <common>\\nuniform float uWet;')\n        .replace('#include <map_fragment>', `#include <map_fragment>\n        // soaked: darker, and the wet cloth a little glossier\n        diffuseColor.rgb *= mix(1.0, 0.7, uWet);`)\n        .replace('#include <roughnessmap_fragment>', `#include <roughnessmap_fragment>\n        roughnessFactor = mix(roughnessFactor, 0.62, uWet);`);\n      dimFillSpecular(shader);\n    }\n  };\n  mat.customProgramCacheKey = () => 'hedgerow-sheet' + (mat.isMeshStandardMaterial ? 's' : 'd');\n}\n\n/* panes: the lit windows in the world (rooms.js paneRects); world, terrain: for the wall in front of\n   each and the ground; shared: the frame's time and wetness */\nexport function createSheets(panes, world, terrain, shared, { count = 4, seed = 41 } = {}) {\n  const R = rng(seed), up = new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0);\n  // an upper-floor window that looks out onto open ground\n  const cand = panes.filter((p) => {\n    if (Math.abs(p.n.y) > 0.2 || p.c.y - terrain.height(p.c.x, p.c.z) < 4.2) return false;\n    const o = p.c.clone().addScaledVector(p.n, 0.6);\n    return !world.raycast(o.x, o.y, o.z, p.n.x, 0, p.n.z, 10);\n  });\n  for (let i = cand.length - 1; i > 0; i--) { const j = Math.floor(R() * (i + 1)); [cand[i], cand[j]] = [cand[j], cand[i]]; }\n  const chosen = [];\n  for (const p of cand) {\n    if (chosen.length >= count) break;\n    if (chosen.some((q) => q.c.distanceTo(p.c) < 14)) continue;\n    chosen.push(p);\n  }\n  if (!chosen.length) return null;\n  const pos = [], uv = [], fold = [], sheet = [], idx = [];\n  chosen.forEach((p, si) => {\n    // the wall's face below the sill: the window is set back in it\n    const below = p.c.clone().addScaledVector(p.B, -(p.hh + 0.35));\n    const o = below.clone().addScaledVector(p.n, 1.5);\n    const hit = world.raycast(o.x, o.y, o.z, -p.n.x, 0, -p.n.z, 3);\n    const face = hit ? Math.max(0.05, 1.5 - hit.t) : 0.15;\n    const w = Math.min(p.hw * 1.8, 1.3), h = 1.2 + R() * 0.5, cell = si % 4, ph = R() * 6.28;\n    const top = p.c.clone().addScaledVector(p.B, -p.hh).addScaledVector(p.n, face + 0.04);\n    const base = pos.length / 3;\n    for (let j = 0; j <= SY; j++) {\n      for (let i = 0; i <= SX; i++) {\n        const u = i / SX, v = j / SY;\n        const q = top.clone().addScaledVector(p.T, (u - 0.5) * w).addScaledVector(up, -v * h);\n        pos.push(q.x, q.y, q.z);\n        uv.push((cell % 2) * 0.5 + u * 0.5, (cell >> 1) * 0.5 + v * 0.5);\n        fold.push(p.n.x, p.n.z, ph, h);\n        sheet.push(u, v);\n      }\n    }\n    for (let j = 0; j < SY; j++) {\n      for (let i = 0; i < SX; i++) {\n        const a = base + j * (SX + 1) + i, b = a + 1, c = a + SX + 1, d = c + 1;\n        idx.push(a, c, b, b, c, d);\n      }\n    }\n  });\n  const geo = new THREE.BufferGeometry();\n  geo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(pos, 3));\n  geo.setAttribute('uv', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(uv, 2));\n  geo.setAttribute('aFold', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(fold, 4));\n  geo.setAttribute('aSheet', new THREE.Float32BufferAttribute(sheet, 2));\n  geo.setIndex(idx);\n  geo.computeVertexNormals();\n  geo.computeBoundingSphere();\n  geo.boundingSphere.radius += 1;\n  const map = linen();\n  const uniforms = { uTime: shared.time, uWet: shared.wet, uWind: { value: new THREE.Vector2(1.6, 0.7) } };\n  const mat = new THREE.MeshStandardMaterial({ map, alphaTest: 0.5, side: THREE.DoubleSide, roughness: 0.92, metalness: 0, flatShading: true });\n  addMotion(mat, uniforms);\n  const mesh = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);\n  mesh.name = 'sheets';\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\n  // its shadow moves with it\n  const dist = new THREE.MeshDistanceMaterial({ map, alphaTest: 0.5, side: THREE.DoubleSide });\n  addMotion(dist, uniforms);\n  mesh.customDistanceMaterial = dist;\n  return { mesh, count: chosen.length, at: chosen.map((p) => p.c) };\n}\n","numLines":188,"startLine":1,"totalLines":188}},"displayPath":"js/cloth.js"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d1e7b30b-2a3a-4e50-85bd-1aad350955bd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:23:15.901Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/