{"parentUuid":"73ac97fd-b6d6-4f76-a2b1-27a0d34c02cd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGL33ENUAcEixHZQMMjs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AA4Qxgjf6CrBYhsjKk1NFS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='js/rooms.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"   ({m, x, y, z, yaw, scale}); each {c, n, T, B, hw, hh} (centre, facing, across, up, half sizes). */\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"   ({m, x, y, z, yaw, scale}); each {c, n, T, B, hw, hh, prop} (centre, facing, across, up, half\n   sizes, and the placement it's in). */\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='js/cloth.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=s[s.index(\"/* panes: the lit windows in the world\"):s.index(\"  const pos = [], uv = [], fold = [], sheet = [], idx = [];\")]\nnew='''/* A house's own surfaces, where it stands (the collision boxes are rougher than its walls). */\nconst houses = new Map(), ray = new THREE.Raycaster();\nfunction house(pr) {\n  let g = houses.get(pr);\n  if (!g) {\n    g = new THREE.Group();\n    for (const prim of pr.m.prims || []) if (prim.geometry) g.add(new THREE.Mesh(prim.geometry));\n    g.position.set(pr.x, pr.y, pr.z);\n    g.rotation.y = pr.yaw || 0;\n    g.scale.setScalar(pr.scale || 1);\n    g.updateMatrixWorld(true);\n    houses.set(pr, g);\n  }\n  return g;\n}\n\n/* What holds a sheet hung from pane p, looking at the house from the street in front of it: the top\n   rail of a railing or the sill, the first thing below the glass that stands out in front of it.\n   Down the wall from there, how far the sheet can hang before something sticks out into it (a shop's\n   sign, a porch roof). Depths along n from the glass (m). */\nfunction hanging(p, w) {\n  const g = house(p.prop), o = new THREE.Vector3(), back = p.n.clone().negate();\n  const depth = (s, u) => {\n    o.copy(p.c).addScaledVector(p.B, s).addScaledVector(p.T, u).addScaledVector(p.n, 2);\n    ray.set(o, back); ray.far = 2.6;\n    const h = ray.intersectObject(g, true)[0];\n    return h ? 2 - h.distance : -1;\n  };\n  const cols = [-0.35 * w, 0, 0.35 * w];\n  const row = (s) => cols.map((u) => depth(s, u));\n  // down the lower part of the window\n  let top = null;\n  for (let s = Math.min(1.1, 2 * p.hh - 0.15) - p.hh; s > -p.hh - 0.3; s -= 0.04) {\n    if (row(s).every((d) => d > 0.05)) { top = s; break; }\n  }\n  if (top === null) return null;\n  const front = Math.max(...row(top), ...row(top - 0.04), ...row(top - 0.08)) + 0.03;\n  let len = 0;\n  for (let s = top - 0.12; s > top - 1.9; s -= 0.05) {\n    if (row(s).some((d) => d > front - 0.01)) break;\n    len = top - s;\n  }\n  return { top, front, len };\n}\n\n/* panes: the lit windows in the world (rooms.js paneRects); world, terrain: for the open ground in\n   front of each, and the ground below; shared: the frame's time and wetness */\nexport function createSheets(panes, world, terrain, shared, { count = 4, seed = 41 } = {}) {\n  const R = rng(seed), up = new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0);\n  // an upper-floor window that looks out onto open ground\n  const cand = panes.filter((p) => {\n    if (!p.prop || Math.abs(p.n.y) > 0.2 || p.c.y - terrain.height(p.c.x, p.c.z) < 4.2) return false;\n    const o = p.c.clone().addScaledVector(p.n, 0.6);\n    return !world.raycast(o.x, o.y, o.z, p.n.x, 0, p.n.z, 10);\n  });\n  for (let i = cand.length - 1; i > 0; i--) { const j = Math.floor(R() * (i + 1)); [cand[i], cand[j]] = [cand[j], cand[i]]; }\n  const chosen = [];\n  for (const p of cand) {\n    if (chosen.length >= count) break;\n    if (chosen.some((q) => q.p.c.distanceTo(p.c) < 14)) continue;\n    const w = Math.min(p.hw * 1.8, 1.3), at = hanging(p, w);\n    if (!at || at.len < 0.9) continue;\n    chosen.push({ p, w, at });\n  }\n  houses.clear();\n  if (!chosen.length) return null;\n'''\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\nold=s[s.index(\"  chosen.forEach((p, si) => {\"):s.index(\"    const base = pos.length / 3;\")]\nnew='''  chosen.forEach(({ p, w, at }, si) => {\n    const h = Math.min(at.len, 1.2 + R() * 0.5), cell = si % 4, ph = R() * 6.28;\n    const top = p.c.clone().addScaledVector(p.B, at.top + 0.02).addScaledVector(p.n, at.front);\n'''\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\ns=s.replace(\"  return { mesh, count: chosen.length, at: chosen.map((p) => p.c) };\",\"  return { mesh, count: chosen.length, at: chosen.map(({ p }) => p.c) };\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncp js/cloth.js $TMPDIR/chk_cloth.mjs && node --check $TMPDIR/chk_cloth.mjs && echo ok; rm -f $TMPDIR/chk_cloth.mjs; sed -n 120,200p js/cloth.js","description":"Place sheets by raycasting the house models"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":640,"cache_read_input_tokens":177788,"output_tokens":2165,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":640,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2165,"cache_read_input_tokens":177788,"cache_creation_input_tokens":640,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":640},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AA4Qxgjf6CrBYhsjKk1NFS":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='js/rooms.js'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"   ({m, x, y, z, yaw, scale}); each {c, n, T, B, hw, hh} (centre, facing, across, up, half sizes). */\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"   ({m, x, y, z, yaw, scale}); each {c, n, T, B, hw, hh, prop} (centre, facing, across, up, half\n   sizes, and the placement it's in). */\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='js