anch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"08e0d213-49d5-4dc6-bcb6-5f7f079ea2d0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017sfcS1DFQvuA9VbtJ1UspE","type":"tool_result","content":"Tried and dropped: water running in the street's gutters (STREET in the ruts texture, a flat\nmirror strip along each cobble edge with downstream wavelets). Placed right, but under this\nlighting a flat dark stream reflecting dark house fronts is indistinguishable from the wet\ncobbles beside it in A/B captures; not worth the shader cost and complexity.\nTried and left out (a taste call for the user): a bleach-bypass grade in post.js (desaturate the\nmid tones, contrast about mid grey). At 0.35 the street gets a silvery Saving-Private-Ryan look,\nbut the night frame sits mostly below mid grey, so the meadow and forest went murky; a lower\npivot would be needed. Left the grade as it was.\nChecked: low and medium quality presets compile and render all the new effects through their\nfallbacks (no late pass: rain/flames/plumes/fireballs with the scene; window light and rain sheets\noff); no shader errors.\n\nTried and shelved: eye adaptation in the grade pass (a 1x1 half-float ping-pong stalls: the\nper-frame step is under half-float resolution; and the flare-lit meadow measures inside the\nnormal night range, so it would not have tamed that glare). WIP copy in the session scratchpad.\n\nObserved, not fixed (pre-existing, invisible): adding or removing any swapping pass in the effects\nchain changes ~150 pixels by 3-7 levels along a hairline of slope 0.75 through (256,0) at\n1024x768 - some pass's rounding depends on buffer parity. Neither parity shows a visible seam.\n\nTried and dropped: raindrops beaded on rifles/outfits (unreadable at this resolution and lighting).\n\nTesting tip: a headless Chrome (playwright's chromium_headless_shell) renders on the real GPU\nwithout the browser pane; driven over CDP from a scratch script (needs the sandbox off to start).\n\nAAA gap list (written to steer the rounds; against what CoD WWII / MoH-class renderers show):\n  Present: PBR + rain wetness everywhere; 2 shadowed point lights (high) + flash shadows; SSAO;\n  SSR; volumetric light, shafts; TAA, motion blur, DOF, bloom, grade/grain/vignette, heat haze,\n  hurt/mud-on-view; rain (streaks, sheets, splashes, crowns, drips, ripples), lightning, flares,\n  dynamic sky with front/searchlights/flak; fog + mist; decals by surface (stone/wood/metal/mud/\n  glass, scorch) + pinned battle damage; particles (muzzle, smoke, sparks, debris lumps, embers,\n  leaves, steam, casings); fire/flames/fireballs; river/ponds/puddles; vegetation wind, grass\n  blades, leaf translucency; skin SSS, cloth sheen, grime; close-up detail (bark, grain, weave,\n  guns); interior mapping behind lit windows.\n  Gaps: (1) asset fidelity - low-poly FP hands/arms, soldiers, chunky props (assets/rig, outside\n  this branch's brief); (2) no bounce light/GI (fires do not light walls indirectly); (3) nothing\n  destructible; (4) no cloth (flags, curtains, tarps); (5) little environment storytelling\n  (signage, posters, painted ads); (6) blood kept minimal (tone call, user); (7) no eye\n  adaptation (shelved); (8) enemies hard to read at night (gameplay call, user).\n- c83f31ec painted wall advertisements (gap 5 of the list above): atmosphere.js wallAd painter +\n  'sign' kind (pinned only, CELL*2, renderOrder 0.5 under spall/holes; canvas drawn flipped about\n  the cell centre since rows run up the wall; canvas system fonts Georgia / Arial Narrow fallbacks,\n  generic trades only). pin(kind, ..., grain, R, upright, variant) - two new optional params.\n  damage.js: SIGN sizes [4.2, 3.7, 3.3] m, up to SIGNS=5, 20 m apart, h 2.6-4.9 m, plaster fit;\n  main.js pinned.sign = 5. Side effect: the sign search draws from the same seeded rng, so the\n  battle-damage layout shifted (still deterministic). 4 signs fit in the level.\n- ca04193d blast rework (effects.js explosion(), fireball.js cool term): new third particle\n  system `thrown` (600, alpha, renderOrder 6.5, moves to the late scene with the additive one in\n  useLate; depthTest follows usePass) for the mud geyser (30 jets) and mud spray (34 streaks);\n  particle `dense` flag (aMisc.w) - VERT dims each light by 0.15-1 by dot(L, toEye) for dense\n  particles. Flash sprite 0.045 s, 1.5-2.6 m. fireball.js cool = smoothstep(0.0, 0.55, t) (was\n  0.04-0.7). Dust ring '#433c33' a0.5. Checked: high, medium, low (no late pass) all render it.\n  Truck fire looked fine up close - left as is.\n- 2a45e2e9 glass shards: decals.paneAt exported; effects.setPaneAt(fn) (main.js passes\n  G.decals.paneAt); effects.impact routes stone/wood hits inside a lit pane to effects.glass()\n  (alpha shards + additive glints) instead of the stone dust. Audio still plays the stone impact\n  (audio.js has no glass foley - a possible follow-up).\n  Reference check attempt: CoD Vanguard \"Operation Tonga\" images on Fandom are hotlink-blocked\n  (403) and the full-size lightbox sits behind a consent wall; Steam store screenshots are behind\n  an age gate (birth date form). Not accepted/entered - comparisons stay from knowledge.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f04b5ed8-abbf-4a1e-86bf-d954d2130069","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:42:23.295Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Tried and dropped: water running in the street's gutters (STREET in the ruts texture, a flat\nmirror strip along each cobble edge with downstream wavelets). Placed right, but under this\nlighting a flat dark stream reflecting dark house fronts is indistinguishable from the wet\ncobbles beside it in A/B captures; not worth the shader cost and complexity.\nTried and left out (a taste call for the user): a bleach-bypass grade in post.js (desaturate the\nmid tones, contrast about mid grey). At 0.35 the street gets a silvery Saving-Private-Ryan look,\nbut the night frame sits mostly below mid grey, so the meadow and forest