{"parentUuid":"b25867d7-01c4-417d-9e27-3fcbb8676279","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGM8gt2iun9YSXS3zWgx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed as 556743c5, and it merges cleanly with hedgerow-poc. Writing the shared notes, then tearing down the test rig."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":295580,"output_tokens":1242,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":38},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":867,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":295580,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":867},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fc94b00e-3cad-4664-890a-4628341fc70a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgGM8gYwN9vveKSPWfPEv","requestRef":"b9e31646-6047-445e-8857-72c176b4f38d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c6c8cc68-dfd7-4834-94cd-2fe3fef33020","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:42:49.823Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"c6c8cc68-dfd7-4834-94cd-2fe3fef33020","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGM8gt2iun9YSXS3zWgx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013dg2eR7s8BRUxXZb1WJZRK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"N=\"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md\"; cat >> \"$N\" <<'EOF'\n- 556743c5 white sheets from the windows (gap 4, cloth; prompted by the MoH Airborne street frame\n  on Wikipedia - a big white cloth hanging over a dusk street): new cloth.js createSheets(panes,\n  world, terrain, shared, {count=4, seed=41}); main.js calls it after setPanes and adds the mesh.\n  rooms.js paneRects now also returns `prop` (the placement) per pane.\n  Placement: candidate panes are vertical, >= 4.2 m over the ground, with open ground 10 m out\n  along n (world.raycast); one per house model first (prop.m), then repeats; 14 m apart. The hang\n  point comes from the house's own triangles (the collision boxes sit ~25 cm behind the real\n  facades - the first try put the sheets inside the walls): every triangle flattened into the\n  pane frame (u across, s up, d out), front-facing only, and depth(s,u) = outermost d. The top is\n  the first row (3 columns) below the glass that stands > 5 cm out (rail or sill); front = max\n  depth there + 3 cm; length runs down until anything reaches the hang plane (max 1.9 m, min 0.9).\n  THREE.Raycaster on the models cost 480 ms at load (0.66 ms a ray); the flattened version 8 ms.\n  Shape: 14x16 quads; pleats (2 sines) 2-5.5 cm, hem curl 4 cm; aDu/aDv rest slopes as\n  attributes; the vertex shader adds sheetMove() (gust() from weather.js, wet = heavier, more\n  lift in the house's lee, sideways along the wind) and gets the normal by finite differences of\n  the move added to the rest slopes. Winding chosen per sheet so front faces face the street\n  (DoubleSide flips back faces). Fold AO from aFold.w. customDistanceMaterial (lamps) and\n  customDepthMaterial (flare sun) carry the same motion; three r185 uses custom shadow\n  materials as given (no clone), so onBeforeCompile survives.\n  Gotcha: `out` is a reserved word in GLSL ES 3.0 - a float named `out` killed the program\n  silently (only the program diagnostics show it).\n  Checked: low/medium/high compile (q_chk2 + sheet programs: standard, distance, depth all\n  runnable), 9 node checks, GPU A/B 0.14-0.28 ms with a sheet filling ~20% of the screen by its\n  lamp. Not done: drips off the hem (a fixed drip point would drift from a hem that swings up to\n  ~15 cm).\nEOF\ntail -3 \"$N\"","description":"Add this round's entry to the shared notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_read_input_tokens":295580,"output_tokens":1242,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":38},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":867,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":295580,"cache_creation_input_tokens":867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":867},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013dg2eR7s8BRUxXZb1WJZRK":{"command":"N=\"/Users/vojta/Library/Application REDACTED.md\"; cat >> \"$N\" <<'EOF'\n- 556743c5 white sheets from the windows (gap 4, cloth; prompted by the MoH Airborne street frame\n  on Wikipedia - a big white cloth hanging over a dusk street): new cloth.js createSheets(panes,\n  world, terrain, shared, {count=4, seed=41}); main.js calls it after setPanes and adds the mesh.\n  rooms.js paneRects now also returns `prop` (the placement) per pane.\n  Placement: candidate panes are vertical, >= 4.2 m over the ground, with open ground 10 m out\n  along n (world.raycast); one per house model first (prop.m), then repeats; 14 m apart. The hang\n  point comes from the house's own triangles (the collision boxes sit ~25 cm behind the real\n  facades - the first try put the sheets inside the walls): every triangle flattened into the\n  pane frame (u across, s up, d out), front-facing only, and depth(s,u) = outermost d. The top is\n  the first row (3 columns) below the glass that stands > 5 cm out (rail or sill); front = max\n  depth there + 3 cm; length runs down until anything reaches the hang plane (max 1.9 m, min 0.9).\n  THREE.Raycaster on the models cost 480 ms at load (0.66 ms a ray); the flattened version 8 ms.\n  Shape: 14x16 quads; pleats (2 sines) 2-5.5 cm, hem curl 4 cm; aDu/aDv rest slopes as\n  attributes; the vertex shader adds sheetMove() (gust() from weather.js, wet = heavier, more\n  lift in the house's lee, sideways along the wind) and gets the normal by finite differences of\n  the move added to the rest slopes. Winding chosen per sheet so front faces face the street\n  (DoubleSide flips back faces). Fold AO from aFold.w. customDistanceMaterial (lamps) and\n  customDepthMaterial (flare sun) carry the same motion; three r185 uses custom shadow\n  materials as given (no clone), so onBeforeCompile survives.\n  Gotcha: `out` is a reserved word in GLSL ES 3.0 - a float named `out` killed the program\n  silently (only the program diagnostics show it).\n  Checked: low/medium/high compile (q_chk2 + sheet programs: standard, distance, depth all\n  runnable), 9 node checks, GPU A/B 0.14-0.28 ms with a sheet filling ~20% of the screen by its\n  lamp. Not done: drips off the hem (a fixed drip point would drift from a hem that swings up to\n  ~15 cm).\nEOF\ntail -3 \"$N\"","description":"Add this round's entry to the shared notes"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"fc94b00e-3cad-4664-890a-4628341fc70a","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgGM8gYwN9vveKSPWfP