{"parentUuid":"c15bb3d9-93df-4878-90c4-0325a3c37073","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QTHdBRNegtvKHe8EAM9EQZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Medal of Honor Airborne Operation Neptune screenshot Normandy village\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Medal of Honor: Airborne\",\"url\":\"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-6026/\"},{\"title\":\"Medal of Honor: Airborne\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/medal-of-honor-airborne/3030-6026/\"},{\"title\":\"Bill Text: NY J02021 | 2019-2020 | General Assembly | Introduced\",\"url\":\"https://www.legiscan.com/NY/text/J02021/2019\"},{\"title\":\"Image Gallery\",\"url\":\"https://www.501csw.usafe.af.mil/News/Photos/igphoto/2000673277/\"},{\"title\":\"www.ramstein.af.mil\",\"url\":\"https://www.ramstein.af.mil/News/Photos/igphoto/2003014515/\"},{\"title\":\"At The Crossroads\",\"url\":\"https://www.jamesdietz.com/?p=91\"},{\"title\":\"An official website of the United States government\",\"url\":\"https://www.ramstein.af.mil/News/Photos/igphoto/2003062109/\"},{\"title\":\"www.nysenate.gov\",\"url\":\"https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/bills/2019/J2021\"},{\"title\":\"March FA\",\"url\":\"https://www.tracesofwar.com/persons/34436/March-FA.htm\"},{\"title\":\"www.superstock.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.superstock.com/asset/air-force-col-bryan-callahan-th-air-ground-operations-wing/6145-54180506\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up any screenshots of the Normandy village level. It did return a description of the game's Operation Neptune mission. In that mission, the player's character is dropped into France and must help take and hold Sainte-Mère-Église before the Normandy beach landings Here Travers in air dropped into France and it is up to Travers and CO to take and hold the Ste. Mere Eglise, before the Normandy beach invasion. That page is a text description, not an image.\n\nFor historical context, one result notes that the village stood right in the middle of route N13, which made it significant to the Normandy landings. The 505th Parachute Infantry Regiment captured its objective, the town of Sainte-Mère-Église.\n\nIf you need actual screenshots, a dedicated image search or the game's press kits would be better sources than this query returned.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"54e08edb-db3a-485c-8185-44051baa92c9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:44:23.726Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Medal of Honor Airborne Operation Neptune screenshot Normandy village","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BwMNkJ7QabvU28VJmpDbvo","content":[{"title":"Medal of Honor: Airborne","url":"https://www.giantbomb.com/games/3030-6026/"},{"title":"Medal of Honor: Airborne","url":"https://giantbomb.com/medal-of-honor-airborne/3030-6026/"},{"title":"Bill Text: NY J02021 | 2019-2020 | General Assembly | Introduced","url":"https://www.legiscan.com/NY/text/J02021/2019"},{"title":"Image Gallery","url":"https://www.501csw.usafe.af.mil/News/Photos/igphoto/2000673277/"},{"title":"www.ramstein.af.mil","url":"https://www.ramstein.af.mil/News/Photos/igphoto/2003014515/"},{"title":"At The Crossroads","url":"https://www.jamesdietz.com/?p=91"},{"title":"An official website of the United States government","url":"https://www.ramstein.af.mil/News/Photos/igphoto/2003062109/"},{"title":"www.nysenate.gov","url":"https://www.nysenate.gov/legislation/bills/2019/J2021"},{"title":"March FA","url":"https://www.tracesofwar.com/persons/34436/March-FA.htm"},{"title":"www.superstock.com","url":"https://www.superstock.com/asset/air-force-col-bryan-callahan-th-air-ground-operations-wing/6145-54180506"}]},"The search didn't turn up any screenshots of the Normandy village level. It did return a description of the game's Operation Neptune mission. In that mission, the player's character is dropped into France and must help take and hold Sainte-Mère-Église before the Normandy beach landings Here Travers in air dropped into France and it is up to Travers and CO to take and hold the Ste. Mere Eglise, before the Normandy beach invasion. That page is a text description, not an image.\n\nFor historical context, one result notes that the village stood right in the middle of route N13, which made it significant to the Normandy landings. The 505th Parachute Infantry Regiment captured its objective, the town of Sainte-Mère-Église.\n\nIf you need actual screenshots, a dedicated image search or the game's press kits would be better sources than this query returned."],"durationSeconds":4.80587037499994,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0d08a418-e85c-4d9c-9735-07baff61aaa6","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"REDACTED","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"REDACTED","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c15bb3d9-93df-4878-90c4-0325a3c37073","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"36ae33bb-893d-4e9d-8651-87cb09a8a6b2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d5c0a1d-fdd5-4db0-8cbd-a5c82a0adcb7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FkQvVxZGLezCRTEBNjNMDc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Call of Duty Vanguard Operation Tonga mission screenshots night Normandy\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"call of duty vanguard\",\"url\":\"https://www.co-op.gg/pc/game/call-of-duty-vanguard\"},{\"title\":\"Call of Duty: Vanguard Screenshots and Trailers\",\"url\":\"https://opencritic.com/game/12073/-/media\"},{\"title\":\"call of duty vanguard video teaser fronte occidentale\",\"url\":\"https://multiplayer.it/notizie/call-of-duty-vanguard-video-teaser-fronte-occidentale.html\"},{\"title\":\"Call of Duty Vanguard le battaglie che lo hanno ispirato\",\"url\":\"https://www.animeclick.it/news/amp/92656-call-of-duty-vanguard-le-battaglie-che-lo-hanno-ispirato.amp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Call of Duty: Vanguard\",\"url\":\"https://callofduty.fandom.com/wiki/Call_of_Duty:_Vanguard?so=search\"},{\"title\":\"First Call Of Duty: Vanguard Pictures Leak Operators And Open Beta\",\"url\":\"https://www.ggrecon.com/articles/vanguard-images-leak/\"},{\"title\":\"92656 call of duty vanguard le battaglie che lo hanno ispirato\",\"url\":\"https://www.animeclick.it/news/92656-call-of-duty-vanguard-le-battaglie-che-lo-hanno-ispirato\"},{\"title\":\"game.watch.impress.co.jp\",\"url\":\"https://game.watch.impress.co.jp/docs/news/1345062.html\"},{\"title\":\"call of duty vanguard 1124352672015863928\",\"url\":\"https://discord.REDACTED\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up any night-time Normandy screenshots from Operation Tonga. It did find some related material:\n\n- **Screenshot galleries:** OpenCritic lists four screenshots and Discord's store page lists eleven, but the snippets don't describe their contents, so I can't confirm whether any show a night scene. (OpenCritic has a Screenshots and Trailers section, and Discord's listing includes screenshots 1 through 11.)\n- **Operation Tonga in the story:** In June 1944, British paratrooper Sergeant Arthur Kingsley takes part in Operation Tonga, where he and the Parachute Regiment help destroy the Melville Gun Battery and several other bridges before the Normandy landings. A Vanguard preview also describes the mission as an operation tied to Overlord and the D-Day landings, carried out by the 6th Airborne Division between June 5 and 7, 1944, which fits a pre-dawn airborne setting, though none of these sources confirm that the game's version is set at night.\n- **Pre-release teaser:** An Italian article reports that a 2021 teaser showed a sign reading \"Merville,\" which it links to the Operation Tonga area, and notes that the game may use an alternate version of WWII. (The sign may refer to Merville-Franceville-Plage, a French commune that was part of Operation Tonga.)\n\nFor actual night-mission images, the best next steps are the official Call of Duty site's media gallery or a dedicated screenshot database, which should show captions or mission names.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a09e5949-0144-4f93-a5a2-56cd7578ce3e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:44:24.284Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Call of Duty Vanguard Operation Tonga mission screenshots night Normandy","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0136HZqfVs37duWawptcSsa9","content":[{"title":"call of duty vanguard","url":"https://www.co-op.gg/pc/game/call-of-duty-vanguard"},{"title":"Call of Duty: Vanguard Screenshots and Trailers","url":"https://opencritic.com/game/12073/-/media"},{"title":"call of duty vanguard video teaser fronte occidentale","url":"https://multiplayer.it/notizie/call-of-duty-vanguard-video-teaser-fronte-occidentale.html"},{"title":"Call of Duty Vanguard le battaglie che lo hanno ispirato","url":"https://www.animeclick.it/news/amp/92656-call-of-duty-vanguard-le-battaglie-che-lo-hanno-ispirato.amp.html"},{"title":"Call of Duty: Vanguard","url":"https://callofduty.fandom.com/wiki/Call_of_Duty:_Vanguard?so=search"},{"title":"First Call Of Duty: Vanguard Pictures Leak Operators And Open Beta","url":"https://www.ggrecon.com/articles/vanguard-images-leak/"},{"title":"92656 call of duty vanguard le battaglie che lo hanno ispirato","url":"https://www.animeclick.it/news/92656-call-of-duty-vanguard-le-battaglie-che-lo-hanno-ispirato"},{"title":"game.watch.impress.co.jp","url":"https://game.watch.impress.co.jp/docs/news/1345062.html"},{"title":"call of duty vanguard 1124352672015863928","url":"https://discord.REDACTED"}]},"The search didn't turn up any night-time Normandy screenshots from Operation Tonga. It did find some related material:\n\n- **Screenshot galleries:** OpenCritic lists four screenshots and Discord's store page lists eleven, but the snippets don't describe their contents, so I can't confirm whether any show a night scene. (OpenCritic has a Screenshots and Trailers section, and Discord's listing includes screenshots 1 through 11.)\n- **Operation Tonga in the story:** In June 1944, British paratrooper Sergeant Arthur Kingsley takes part in Operation Tonga, where he and the Parachute Regiment help destroy the Melville Gun Battery and several other bridges before the Normandy landings. A Vanguard preview also describes the mission as an operation tied to Overlord and the D-Day landings, carried out by the 6th Airborne Division between June 5 and 7, 1944, which fits a pre-dawn airborne setting, though none of these sources confirm that the game's version is set at night.\n- **Pre-release teaser:** An Italian article reports that a 2021 teaser showed a sign reading \"Merville,\" which it links to the Operation Tonga area, and notes that the game may use an alternate version of WWII. (The sign may refer to Merville-Franceville-Plage, a French commune that was part of Operation Tonga.)\n\nFor actual night-mission images, the best next steps are the official Call of Duty site's media gallery or a dedicated screenshot database, which should show captions or mission names."],"durationSeconds":6.406952875003219,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0d08a418-e85c-4d9c-9735-07baff61aaa6","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"REDACTED","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"voho/protocodus.github.io","visibility":"public"}]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"REDACTED","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"36ae33bb-893d-4e9d-8651-87cb09a8a6b2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"REDACTED","sessionId":"c33bf617-35bd-4ff6-a907-5e7d748d7fbc","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"shimmying-swimming-falcon"}
