{"parentUuid":"b6bc9bd7-4de0-4cc8-a918-18ce4224a880","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGNJN65je3mYBoJi6dxE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011RBoscEMUmTRUKN1BK3ijN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass/fun/hedgerow && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"    motion and its shading worked out in the vertex shader, its shadow\n    moving with it),\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"    motion and its shading worked out in the vertex shader, its shadow\n    moving with it), `signs.js` (the occupiers' direction posts where the\n    roads meet — by the lane, in the square under the lamp by the church,\n    at the north end of the street and at the camp: a leaning square post\n    crowded with five to eight boards, most of them arrows pointing down\n    their roads, each at its own height and length and a little askew —\n    the towns and how far, the way to the town major, the field police,\n    the dressing station, a command post, the fuel, and the warnings\n    \"Achtung! Feindeinsicht\", \"Staub bringt Tod!\"; painted yellow, white or\n    black and lettered in condensed road-sign capitals, chipped to the grey\n    wood, streaked by the rain, now and then shot through; cut with their\n    thickness, reading the right way from either side, wet like the rest;\n    levelBuild keeps the signpost model's collider and leaves the drawing\n    to it),\n\"\"\"\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd /Users/vojta/Dev/protocodus.github.io/.claude/worktrees/hedgerow-grass && git status --short && git diff --stat","description":"Describe the signposts in the README and review changes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2184,"cache_read_input_tokens":42